@startuml uc-pat-01-comm-alt-a5
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8

title UC-PAT-01: Manage My Appointments (C5 v1.1.0)\nCommunication Diagram - Alternative Flow A5: Action Outside the Policy Window

actor ":Patient" as pat
boundary ":MyAppointmentsUI" as ui
control ":PatientAppointmentController" as ctrl
control ":PatientAppointmentService" as srv
control ":AccessControlService (C1)" as c1
entity ":Booking" as booking
control ":AppointmentRules" as rules
control ":BookingPolicyGateway" as bp
control ":AuditService (C1)" as audit

pat -- ui : 1: chooseConfirm() or confirmCancellation(reason) >\n< 6: displayRejectionAndServiceContact(serviceContact)

ui -- ctrl : 2: POST my-appointments/{bookingId}/confirm or /cancel >\n< 5: HTTP 409 (BOOKING_CONFLICT)

ctrl -- srv : 3: confirmAppointment(...) or cancelAppointment(...) >\n< 4: throw BookingConflictException

srv -- c1 : 3.1: canManageOwnAppointments(actorId, role) >

srv -- booking : 3.2: isOwnedBy(actorId) >

srv -- rules : 3.3: checkConfirm(...) or checkCancel(...) -> [deadline passed] >

rules -- bp : 3.3.1: minHoursBeforeConfirmation() or minHoursBeforeCancellation() >

srv -- audit : 3.4: recordEvent(APPOINTMENT_ACTION_REJECTED, outside policy window) >

note bottom of booking
  The appointment is not changed.
  Normally the button is already hidden by allowedActions (step 5);
  this is the server check when the deadline passes while the page is open.
  The UI shows the serviceContact it received in the details (step 6).
end note
@enduml
